# On layouts/collision.jsonc the Mover is ordered to a point 15 short of the spot where the Holder stands (the click
# refuses a point on the Holder itself). Both fly at the middle of the combat band. The Mover turns about, flies toward the
# point, and meets the Holder's shield surface before it is within tooCloseToTurn of the point; the collision separation
# pushes it back out and up, which leaves it inside that radius in 3D, and its brake spring slows it below half its impulse
# speed; the Mover rests with its order ended (move=none) at speed 0, about 19 from its point and 15.7 above the Holder's
# height, and both rest apart. The dumps cannot tell the push ending the order from an arrival just before or after the
# push; the unit test
# CollisionSeparationTests.AShipOrderedOntoTheSpotWhereAnotherHoldsIsSeparatedEndsItsOrderAndBothRestApart shows the
# push route ending it.
# Dumps: "before" shows them 100 apart at one height; "driving" the Mover on its way with move=<x>,<z>; "contact" the
# state after the contact, with move=none and the Mover 15.7 above the Holder's height, off its point and about 25 from
# the Holder in the plane; "after" and "later" (10 s on) show both still at rest at the same positions.
# Run it with --layout layouts/collision.jsonc; the layout's header comment has the whole command.
# The point is in the frame of the dump's pos= field, whose z is the layout z mirrored.
wait 1
dump before
select Mover
wait 0.3
move 2000 -1915
wait 5
dump driving
wait 3
dump contact
wait 25
dump after
wait 10
dump later
